Chris,

I think you aren't using the right geom for the job here, but I'm not entirely sure.

Does this give you more of what you're after?

ggplot(group1, aes(x = LME, y = as.Date(as.character(Year), format="%Y"),  fill = Correlate)) + geom_tile() + scale_y_date() + coord_flip()

HTH,

B

On Tue, Aug 13, 2013 at 1:30 PM, chris mcowen <chris...@gmail.com> wrote:

>
> Dear List,
>
> I am trying to make a stacked bar chart with a mapped value to the y aesthetic.
>
> ggplot(group1, aes(x = LME, y = Year,  fill = Correlate)) + geom_bar(stat = "identity") + coord_flip()
>
> The problem I am having is the values on the y axis (year) comes out as the sum of the series, rather than as discrete years. (1959,1960,1961 etc).
>
> I have played about changing the year to a factor, integer and number but this doesn't help,  I have a feeling it may have something to do with the way stat_identity behaves but i am unsure?
